18:["$","aside",null,{"className":"docs_toc__B_lbZ","aria-label":"On this page","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"ON THIS PAGE"}],[["$","a","make-api-instances-interchangeable",{"href":"#make-api-instances-interchangeable","children":"Make API instances interchangeable"}],["$","a","worked-bottleneck-comparison",{"href":"#worked-bottleneck-comparison","children":"Worked bottleneck comparison"}],["$","a","diagram-add-instances-at-the-bottleneck",{"href":"#diagram-add-instances-at-the-bottleneck","children":"Diagram: add instances at the bottleneck"}],["$","a","implementation-route-to-interchangeable-instances",{"href":"#implementation-route-to-interchangeable-instances","children":"Implementation: route to interchangeable instances"}],["$","a","engineering-exercise",{"href":"#engineering-exercise","children":"Engineering exercise"}],["$","a","design-review-questions",{"href":"#design-review-questions","children":"Design review questions"}],["$","a","read-further",{"href":"#read-further","children":"Read further"}]]]}]
19:["$","main",null,{"className":"docs_main__7o2m6","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_articleMeta__8zYHO","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"LESSON 03 OF 10"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Systems"}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"docs_article__Ja_Vh","children":[["$","$1","0",{"children":[[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Scaling and load balancing"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Vertical scaling"}]," gives one machine more CPU, memory, or I/O capacity. ",["$","strong","strong-1",{"children":"Horizontal scaling"}]," adds machines or processes. Either may help, but only at the current bottleneck. Two API instances do not double throughput when both wait on the same saturated database."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"make-api-instances-interchangeable","children":"Make API instances interchangeable"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["A load balancer distributes incoming connections among healthy API instances. The API should keep durable state in the database or object store, not solely in one process's memory. Store browser session state in a signed token or shared session store according to the security model; do not require “sticky” routing just to find an editor's document. Health checks remove an instance that cannot serve traffic, while ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"draining"}]," lets existing requests finish before a rollout or scale-down. A health check should reflect the dependencies needed for the endpoint, without causing every transient dependency blip to restart every instance."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"Autoscaling adds or removes instances based on a signal such as CPU, request rate, or queue depth. The signal must relate to the bottleneck, and the policy needs warm-up, bounds, and cooldown. Scaling from two to twenty API instances can accidentally create hundreds of new database connections; the connection budget is a separate design decision."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"id":"worked-bottleneck-comparison","children":"Worked bottleneck comparison"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"At peak, an API fleet has CPU at 85%, database CPU at 30%, and p99 latency rises with API request queueing. More API instances may help. In another peak, API CPU is 25% and database connections are maxed out. More API instances may worsen contention. Measure per-stage latency, saturation, error rate, and p99 while changing one variable. Run a load test using a realistic mix of opens, edits, and searches rather than one cheap endpoint."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"id":"diagram-add-instances-at-the-bottleneck","children":"Diagram: add instances at the bottleneck"}],"\n",["$","figure","p-4",{"className":"docs_studyFigure__4Js_y","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"docs_studyFigureViewport__ZYDNN","children":["$","img","img-0",{"className":"docs_studyFigureImage__Gb2YJ","src":"/learning/scale-design/scaling.svg","alt":"A load balancer routes readers across healthy API instances; all instances share a database, whose connection limit remains a shared constraint.","width":"920","height":"402","loading":"lazy"}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"children":"A load balancer routes readers across healthy API instances; all instances share a database, whose connection limit remains a shared constraint."}]]}],"\n",["$","details","pre-0",{"className":"docs_textDiagram__KfHuf","children":[["$","summary",null,{"children":"Read the text version of this flow"}],["$","pre",null,{"children":["$","code","code-0",{"className":"language-aosdf-diagram","children":"Readers ──▶ load balancer ──▶ API A ─┐\n                          └──▶ API B ─┼──▶ shared database\n                          └──▶ API C ─┘\n"}]}]]}],"\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31"],false]}]]}],"$L32"]}]
